1
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:12,116
Hello, friends!

2
00:00:12,166 --> 00:00:15,873
Welcome back to Grandpa Sol's porch.

3
00:00:15,923 --> 00:00:23,702
Today a little boy next door fell off his bike, and Eli ran to help him up.

4
00:00:23,752 --> 00:00:28,086
Zara asked, "Grandpa, who is my neighbor?"

5
00:00:28,136 --> 00:00:34,453
So I said, come sit close, and I'll tell you what Jesus said.

6
00:00:34,503 --> 00:00:40,430
One day a teacher of the law asked Jesus a big question.

7
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:46,406
Jesus said, "Love the Lord your God with all your heart.

8
00:00:46,456 --> 00:00:51,209
And love your neighbor as you love yourself."

9
00:00:51,259 --> 00:00:55,477
The man asked, "And who is my neighbor?"

10
00:00:55,527 --> 00:00:57,825
So Jesus told a story.

11
00:00:57,875 --> 00:01:04,869
A man was walking down a long, dusty road from Jerusalem to Jericho.

12
00:01:04,919 --> 00:01:07,873
Suddenly, robbers jumped out!

13
00:01:07,923 --> 00:01:12,534
They took his things, hurt him, and ran away.

14
00:01:12,584 --> 00:01:18,542
The poor man lay beside the road, and he could not get up.

15
00:01:18,592 --> 00:01:23,232
Soon a priest came walking down the road.

16
00:01:23,282 --> 00:01:25,520
He saw the hurt man.

17
00:01:25,570 --> 00:01:27,809
But he did not stop.

18
00:01:27,859 --> 00:01:33,415
He crossed to the other side and kept on walking.

19
00:01:33,465 --> 00:01:40,116
Then a Levite came along, a man who worked at God's temple.

20
00:01:40,166 --> 00:01:42,842
He saw the hurt man too.

21
00:01:42,892 --> 00:01:45,909
But he did not stop either.

22
00:01:45,959 --> 00:01:51,475
He crossed to the other side and kept on walking.

23
00:01:51,525 --> 00:01:56,376
Next came a man from Samaria, called a Samaritan.

24
00:01:56,426 --> 00:01:59,977
Many people did not like Samaritans.

25
00:02:00,027 --> 00:02:05,579
But when the Samaritan saw him, his heart felt very sad.

26
00:02:05,629 --> 00:02:06,879
He felt pity.

27
00:02:06,929 --> 00:02:09,577
The Samaritan ran to him!

28
00:02:09,627 --> 00:02:16,050
He poured oil and wine on the hurt places to help them heal.

29
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:20,690
Then he wrapped them up with soft bandages.

30
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:24,756
He lifted the man onto his own donkey.

31
00:02:24,806 --> 00:02:27,217
Clip, clop, clip, clop!

32
00:02:27,267 --> 00:02:35,563
They went slowly to an inn, and the Samaritan took care of him all night long.

33
00:02:35,613 --> 00:02:42,806
In the morning, the Samaritan gave two silver coins to the innkeeper.

34
00:02:42,856 --> 00:02:47,004
"Please take care of this man," he said.

35
00:02:47,054 --> 00:02:53,092
"If it costs more, I will pay you back when I come again."

36
00:02:53,142 --> 00:03:01,696
Then Jesus asked, "Which of the three was a neighbor to the man the robbers hurt?"

37
00:03:01,746 --> 00:03:06,208
The teacher said, "The one who helped him."

38
00:03:06,258 --> 00:03:10,090
And Jesus said, "Go and do the same."

39
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:21,079
So a neighbor is anyone who needs our help, and we can be kind to everyone, even when it is not easy.

40
00:03:21,129 --> 00:03:28,150
You can share, help, and say kind words, just like the Samaritan.

41
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:32,831
Now let's sing Be a Good Neighbor together.

42
00:03:32,881 --> 00:03:39,797
Give a big helping hug to someone next to you, with Eli and Pip!

43
00:03:39,847 --> 00:03:40,450
Ready?

44
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:41,430
Let's go!
